  "summary": [
    "D12 (first stage of the colour-class promotion) turns the six X34/X212/X23 helpers edge_colour_rel and colour_graph into aliases of GTBase.edge_colourings.edge_colour_class_rel col (pred1 i) and edge_colour_class col (pred1 i), the Extremal area colour-class contract promoted under distinct names; headers and implicit arguments unchanged, no guard.",
    "Frozen at the D10 pin in <area>/theories/migration/edge_colour_class.v: the six sources and the six opaque symmetry/irreflexivity lemmas with their original scripts (relation renamed to Legacy), the linear-forest and linear-arboricity chains and the three rows; the six live lemmas keep their headers and are proved by the canonical lemmas. Graph certificates are adjacency equality, the identity isomorphism and its identity carrier map.",
    "Four whole iff, kernel-checked: the three current rows by conversion (is_forest and Delta read only carrier and adjacency), and the complete X34 Original over M1's frozen raw edge set at 061154c (same colouring for the widened linear-forest colours and the ord_max matching, exact let q, planar / odd / 9 <= Delta guards with the documented 9-vs-7 defect kept). X212 and X23 keep the supplied colouring, attained minimum and universal minimality.",
    "Extremal.foundations.edge_colourings.colour_class is the same contract; its public adapter, old C6 snapshots and history are the next stage of this family (pending_adapters), so the promotion is not complete."
  ],
  "kernel_evidence": "Exact types/implicit status of the six sources and six lemmas, the four whole iff, all old declarations against 2f37b10a, the 323 reverse headers of the 23-file closure, Print Assumptions, About-resolved strict closures (frozen/live/M1) and negatives, through the pinned image. /srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/D12-by-lancelot/ (outside the repository)",
  "pending_adapters": [
